-#
-#  The complete bookings browser: the generic CNF filter + the bookings table,
-#  both rendered by the shared widget (shared/_expandable_table via
-#  fin/bookings/_bookings_table). Everything about the filter's CONTENT and
-#  STATE -- the catalog, the applied conditions, the pinned ones and their
-#  labels, the pane, the reset URL, the carried params -- comes from the table's
-#  state, i.e. from the controller's wsjrdp_expandable_table_policy. What is
-#  left here are display options. Hosts render it with:
-#    rows:          the bookings Wsjrdp::ExpandableTableRows of the host
-#                   (Fin::BookingsController#bookings,
-#                   Fin::ReconciliationController#bookings)
-#    apply_url:     POST target of the filter builder (PRG)
-#    condensed_locked:  show the pinned conditions as a compact summary line
-#    extra_columns: injected table columns (e.g. the match-proposal column)
-#    selection:, detail_top:, detail_extra:  passed to the table
- filter_cfg = {apply_url: apply_url,
    condensed_locked: local_assigns.fetch(:condensed_locked, false),
    disabled: local_assigns.fetch(:disabled, false)}
= render "fin/bookings/bookings_table", rows: rows, filter: filter_cfg,
  extra_columns: local_assigns[:extra_columns],
  selection: local_assigns[:selection], detail_top: local_assigns[:detail_top],
  detail_extra: local_assigns[:detail_extra]
